# Cloudflare Pages fallback rules (copied to dist/ by Vite).
# Docs: developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# SPA fallback: unmatched paths must render the app so a deep link or a refresh
# on /deals or /profile survives. This rule runs before the 404 handler and
# matches everything, including /assets/, so it is not the only thing that
# decides what a missing asset returns.
#
# A missing asset must not land here. A URL ever answered with 200 + text/html
# gets cached under the `/assets/*` rule in `_headers` (`immutable`, one year),
# so the browser keeps reading HTML as a module or a stylesheet long after the
# real file is back. Cloudflare Pages answers unmatched requests under /assets/
# with a real 404 instead (`no-store`, at any depth), because the stub at
# public/assets/404.html exists — that stub, not a rule here, is what keeps
# asset misses uncacheable.
#
# Do not add a rule matching /assets/* to fix anything: `_redirects` supports
# redirects (301/302/303/307/308) and 200 proxying only, never a 404, so the
# only rule available would rewrite the miss to something the edge can cache —
# and it would run first and shadow the stub. `npm run build` fails if one
# appears; see scripts/check-pages-fallbacks.mjs.

